===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|person}} A [[person#Noun|person]] who [[cut#Verb|cuts]] and [[polish#Verb|polishes]], [[engrave]]s, or [[deal#Verb|deals]] in [[gem#Noun|gems]] and [[precious stone]]s.
#: {{synonyms|en|gemsmith|lapidarist|lapidist<q:obsolete, rare>}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Peter G. Read|title=Gemmology|year=2013|page=289|publisher=Elsevier|passage=In the very early days of gemstone fashioning, a polisher or '''lapidary''' would cut and polish both diamonds and other gemstones.}}
# The [[field#Noun|field]] in which such a person [[work#Verb|works]], a [[subfield]] of [[gemology]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}}
## An [[expert#Noun|expert]] in gems and precious stones; a [[connoisseur]] of lapidary work.
##: {{synonyms|en|lapidist<q:obsolete, rare>}}
## {{senseid|en|jewellery}} Gems and precious stones [[collectively]]; [[jewellery]].
## {{senseid|en|treatise}}{{lb|en|except|historical}} A [[treatise]] on ([[precious#Adjective|precious]]) [[stone#Noun|stones]].

